# Agent transcripts. Large, machine written, never source.
*.jsonl

# Generated by tsc --noEmit. Not source.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

__pycache__/

# Measurements from tools/raster_lab.py and tools/raster_fidelity.py. They are
# reproducible from those two scripts, and the contact sheets include samples
# rendered from the system Arial, which is Apple's to license and not ours to
# commit. The conclusions drawn from them live in TYPOGRAPHY-REPORT.md.
tools/raster-lab-out/

# Scratch build directories from a verification build run with NEXT_DIST_DIR,
# so a build check cannot overwrite the .next a running server is reading.
#
# The glob is deliberate: the previous entry named one specific directory
# (.next-verify/) while the check builds were actually writing to
# .next-hybrid-review/, so the scratch tree was left untracked-but-unignored
# and showed up as noise in every status. Matching the prefix covers whatever
# NEXT_DIST_DIR is set to next time.
#
# Anchored at the repository root, and the trailing slash means directories
# only — no source file can be hidden by it, and `.next` itself is matched by
# its own rule above rather than by this one.
/.next-*/

# Local configuration. .env.example is the documented, committed template; the
# real values — paths on this machine, coordinates, an origin or two — stay
# here and out of git. They are not secrets, but they are nobody else's
# business and they would be wrong on every other machine.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# The public snapshot tools/public-snapshot.sh builds. Regenerate it; never
# commit a copy of the repository into the repository.
/public-snapshot/

# Internal briefs, reports and plans.
#
# These were tracked. They are the working material of the project and worth
# keeping — they are also full of one household's LAN address, absolute paths
# under one home directory, a calendar name, and the owner's first name. None of
# that belongs in a repository that is meant to be published, and none of it
# should be deleted either. So they are untracked (`git rm --cached`, never
# `rm`) and ignored from here on: every one of them is still on disk, exactly
# where it was.
#
# tools/public-snapshot.sh also lists them by name. Two mechanisms on purpose:
# this one stops them being re-added by `git add -A`, that one stops them
# reaching a snapshot even if this one is ever loosened.
/FABLE-PLANNING-BRIEF.md
/IMPLEMENTATION-BRIEF.md
/MODULE-EXPANSION-BRIEF.md
/MODULE-EXPANSION-REPORT.md
/TYPOGRAPHY-COMPLETION-BRIEF.md
/TYPOGRAPHY-FOLLOWUP-BRIEF.md
/TYPOGRAPHY-REPORT.md
/RUNBOOK-REAL-PUSH.md

# Planning notes for this and neighbouring projects. Private for the same
# reasons, and the directory is a workspace rather than a document set.
/.hermes/
